  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">A Light on my Path - support for children, youth and the elderly in El Salvador</narrative>
  </title>
  <description>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">The project A Light on my Path intends to create opportunities for learning for children and young people from the violent and poor La Chacra area. It will be offered to them various workshops that will enable them to develop new skills and talents, as they participate in the different activities that will be implemented with the project,  Despite the difficulties that arise daily in families within the community due to the social, economical and political environment they live in, it is intended that this project will foster an atmosphere of harmony, respect and peace in an area formed by several communities in a marginal urban area of San Salvador, through psychological support, a united family programme, the implementation of different workshops, entertainment and learning activities for children, young people and adults. 
The workshops will also be open to children from other educational centres and the community itself who wish to join in the activities that will take place. 
Visits to the elderly who find it difficult to attend training meetings will be strengthened.
The family programme will be applied to various communities in the area and the following topics will be developed: united family, assertive communication, interpersonal relationships, conflict resolution, anger management, self, grief management, psychological first aid to deal with crises that may develop in families and in the community.</narrative>
  </description>
